stream
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 730 Tm
([Model Architecture & Scaled Dot-Product Attention]) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 702 Tm
(3.2 Attention: An attention function can be described as mapping a query and a set) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 687 Tm
(of key-value pairs to an output, where the query, keys, values, and output are all) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 672 Tm
(vectors. We call our particular attention Scaled Dot-Product Attention. The input) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 657 Tm
(consists of queries and keys of dimension d_k, and values of dimension d_v.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 624 Tm
(We compute the dot products of the query with all keys, divide each by the square) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 609 Tm
(root of d_k \(1 / sqrt\(d_k\) scaling factor\), and apply a softmax function to obtain) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 594 Tm
(the weights on the values. For large values of d_k, the dot products grow large in) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 579 Tm
(magnitude, pushing the softmax function into regions where it has extremely small) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 564 Tm
(gradients.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 531 Tm
(Multi-Head Attention allows the model to jointly attend to information from) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 516 Tm
(different representation subspaces at different positions. With a single attention) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 501 Tm
(head, averaging inhibits this. In this work we employ h = 8 parallel attention) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 486 Tm
(layers, or heads, with d_k = d_v = d_model / h = 64.) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
